#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Fulqrum](https://github.com/Qiskit/fulqrum) is a software package that "
"computes eigenvalues and eigenvectors of Hamiltonians projected into a "
"subspace. It constructs a portable representation of the projected "
"Hamiltonian that you can pass to an eigenvalue solver of your choice, "
"including standard off-the-shelf solvers. These solvers can provide a much "
"faster alternative to the default PySCF solver that the SQD addon uses for "
"diagonalization. For information on how to install and use Fulqrum, see the "
"[Fulqrum documentation](https://qiskit.github.io/fulqrum/).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Fulqrum's `addon_sqd_support` module builds a solver that "
"[`diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"addon-sqd/fermion) accepts directly, so you pass the same integrals to both "
"and Fulqrum handles the projection and diagonalization.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For more details on the SQD code used in this example, see the [chemistry "
"Hamilton tutorial](/tutorials/sample-based-quantum-diagonalization).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Use a different eigensolver {#use-a-different-eigensolver}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because Fulqrum exposes the projected Hamiltonian as a standard "
"[`scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator.html),"
" you can diagonalize it with any eigensolver of your choosing rather than "
"being tied to `scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh`. This makes it straightforward to "
"substitute a solver that is better suited to your problem size or "
"hardware.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Pass the eigensolver you want as the `eigensolver` argument. As an example, "
"this guide demonstrates [PRIMME](https://github.com/primme/primme), a high-"
"performance eigensolver library. Its Python interface, `primme.eigsh`, "
"follows a calling convention similar to `scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh`, so you "
"can use it as a direct replacement.\n"
msgstr ""
